From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:16:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Require Go 1.25 for the x/text fix to GO-2026-5970

govulncheck finds GO-2026-5970 (CVE-2026-56852) reachable from this
module: golang.org/x/text v0.34.0, the version aontu/go requires, can loop
forever in unicode/norm on invalid UTF-8, and model generation reaches it
through AontuResolver.Resolve -> Aontu.Generate -> norm.Form.Properties.
A model file saved in a legacy encoding is invalid UTF-8, so this is not
only an attack surface.

The fix is in x/text v0.39.0, and every fixed release declares go 1.25.0,
so the module's go line moves from 1.24.7 to 1.25.0 and x/text goes to
v0.41.0, the newest release that still declares 1.25.0. x/mod goes to
v0.40.0 alongside it, which clears GO-2026-6179 and GO-2026-6180 (sumdb,
imported but not called). Under a current toolchain govulncheck now
reports no vulnerabilities. Go 1.24 and 1.25 are both past end of life,
and a consumer on 1.24 with the default GOTOOLCHAIN=auto gets 1.25
fetched for them.

CI tests the declared minimum, so build.yml and publish.yml move from Go
1.24 to 1.25. AGENTS.md, the README and the reference now state Go 1.25.

aontu/go itself still declares go 1.24.7. Dropping this commit keeps Go
1.24 support and leaves the advisory open until aontu/go moves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
